  Debug-only network policy for the ping_davinci integration-test host.

  The hermetic integration-test mode starts an in-process HttpServer inside the test process and
  points the SDK at it over plain HTTP, which Android blocks by default (API 28+).

  This is a base-config, not a loopback-only domain-config, on purpose. The Ping Android SDK's
  Ktor CIO engine validates TLS through the two-argument X509TrustManager.checkServerTrusted, and
  Android's NetworkSecurityTrustManager rejects that call outright ("Domain specific configurations
  require that hostname aware checkServerTrusted ... is used") as soon as any domain-config exists.
  A loopback domain-config would therefore break every HTTPS request, so live mode against a real
  tenant could never work. Certificates are still validated normally against the system trust
  anchors; this only permits http:// in addition.

  This file lives in src/debug/ and is therefore never merged into a release build.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
